+# Story RC3.3: Referee Form Session — Open, Answer, Autosave
+
+Status: review
+
+Epic: RC3 (Reference-Checking — Messaging & Collection) · Story key: `rc3-3-referee-form-session-open-answer-autosave`
+Sprint: refcheck-v1 (tracker: `_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/sprint-status-refcheck-v1.yaml`)
+
+## Story
+
+As a referee,
+I want to open the link and answer one question at a time with my progress saved,
+so that I can finish in minutes on my phone without an account, or step away and resume.
+
+## Scope (what THIS story owns — and what it does NOT)
+
+**Owns (the form session + its route registration):**
+
+1. **Route registration (AD-3 checklist, incl. the Perkins r1 fix from #595):** `/reference/:token` registered in all three places — `middleware.redact_token_route` (**new `/reference` arm: Sentry/access-log/CSP redaction** — the Perkins r1 warning on rc3-2: the registry claimed to cover `/reference/*` in the spec but had no arm), `middleware.is_public_path`, router arms.
+2. **The form session itself:** landing screen (second Art 14 moment + both escape routes before any question), per-slot question sets (previous-landlord 11, employer 8, character 5), one-question-per-screen on mobile with progress, single `max-w-[48rem]` page on desktop, as-stated checks pre-filled **where application data actually exists** (see the data-availability matrix — a disk-truth deviation from the UX presumption).
+3. **Autosave + resume (A2):** `PUT /reference/:token/answer` (JS) + equivalent per-question `POST` (no-JS — SSR never requires JS), persisting to `draft_answers` JSONB; re-opening resumes at the next unanswered question.
+4. **Token-state branded pages** (unknown / expired / completed / declined / landlord-handling — UX §8.5, truthful + distinct, no dead ends) and the **expired-link "Send me a new link" resend flow** (re-mints the token, re-sends to the contact on file, audit-logged).
+5. **`form_opened_at` stamping** on first live-form GET (AD-10's `completion_seconds` input).
+6. **Abuse posture (AD-15):** honeypot field + submission-timing validation on the answer POSTs (the `/apply`-class posture, reusing `application_handler.is_honeypot_filled`/`is_timing_suspicious`).
+7. **`/static/reference_form.js`** — progressive-enhancement autosave/stepper (CommonJS-exportable pure internals for `node --test`, the `form_draft.js` precedent) **plus its `.gitignore` whitelist entry** (the recurring static-asset review finding — 3 prior sightings).
+
+**Does NOT own (later stories — do not build them):**
+
+- **Final submit, result structuring, thank-you screen, notifications, one-submission enforcement** → **rc3-4**. rc3-3's all-answered review screen renders the Submit button as a forward link to `POST /reference/:token` (404s until rc3-4; unreachable by real users because no `form_token` is minted before rc3-5).
+- **The exit routes** `/reference/:token/decline`, `/reference/:token/stop`, `/reference/:token/wrong-person` → **rc3-4**. rc3-3's landing screen and Q1-No render forward links to them (same pattern as rc3-2's templates linking to this story's route). The URL paths pinned here are the contract rc3-4 implements.
+- **Token minting at T0 + `form_token_expires_at` initial stamp + the cadence sweep** → **rc3-5** (rc3-2 decision 1). rc3-3 mints ONLY in the referee-requested resend flow.
+- **Fraud-signal computation** (`form_session.*`, AD-10) → **rc3-7**. rc3-3 only stamps `form_opened_at` and carries the `_focus_seconds` hidden field through the pages (rc3-4 reads it at submit).
+- **Landlord panel states** ("Form opened" etc.) → **rc4-x** (reads the columns rc3-3 writes).
+- **No migration, no enum changes** — every column (`draft_answers`, `form_opened_at`, `form_token_expires_at`, …) exists since RC2.1; `audit_log.event_type` is unconstrained TEXT (`00000000000001_initial_schema.sql`), so the new audit variant needs no DDL.
+
+## Acceptance Criteria (BDD — from epics, A-register applied)
+
+**AC1 — Route registration + the Perkins r1 fix.**
+Given the AD-3 checklist, when `/reference/:token` ships, then it is registered in all three places: `middleware.redact_token_route` gains a `["reference", ..]` arm (Sentry events, access-log lines, and CSP-report URLs redact the token — the Perkins r1 warning on #595 is closed), `middleware.is_public_path` gains the `/reference` arm, and the router gains the arms in the route table below. The token is ~288-bit (`wisp.random_string(48)`, the `insert_erasure_token` precedent) with RC2.1's unique partial index. Middleware regression tests pin both new arms.
+
+**AC2 — Valid token on a live row → landing.**
+Given a valid token on a live row (`status='contact_initiated'`, not expired), when `GET /reference/:token` runs, then the first live-form GET stamps `form_opened_at` (guarded `SET ... WHERE form_opened_at IS NULL`; never re-stamped, never stamped on state pages), and the landing screen renders per UX §6.5: the second Art 14 moment (context, purpose, retention, notice link `/privacy#referee-data`) plus both escape routes (wrong person, decline) BEFORE any question. Copy per the pinned strings below (UX-verbatim modulo the em-dash ban + slot-neutral phrasing, the rc3-2 deviation conventions).
+
+**AC3 — Per-slot question sets + progress + pre-fill.**
+Given the landing Start, when questions render, then they follow the per-slot sets (previous-landlord 11, employer 8, character 5 — pinned tables below), one per screen on mobile with progress (`aria-label="Question 4 of 11"`), a single `max-w-[48rem]` scrolling page on desktop, and as-stated checks pre-fill per the data-availability matrix. Full-width tappable rows (`h-12` minimum), no paste-blocking, visible amber focus ring (UX §11/§12).
+
+**AC4 — Autosave + resume.**
+Given a referee answering, when each answer is given, then it persists to `draft_answers` via one guarded JSONB-merge UPDATE (live-row guard) — `PUT /reference/:token/answer` with JS (JSON body), `POST /reference/:token/answer` without JS (303 → next question). Re-opening the link with a non-empty draft resumes at the next unanswered question (resumable until submitted). Terminal/stand-down writes never resurrect a row.
+
+**AC5 — Unknown/expired/terminal token → branded pages + resend.**
+Given an unknown, expired, or terminal token, when the page is requested, then the branded pages per the state matrix render with distinct truthful copy (unknown / expired / already completed / declined / landlord handling), 404 for unknown, no dead ends. An expired link on a still-open check (`contact_initiated`, not taken over) offers "Send me a new link" (`POST /reference/:token/resend`): re-mints the token, stamps a fresh 10-day `form_token_expires_at` (A3), re-sends the invite to the effective contact on file via rc3-2's `send_invite`, and writes an audit row (new `ReferenceCallLinkResent` event). Link TTL is 10 days from invitation.
+
+**AC6 — Abuse posture (AD-15).**
+Given the answer/resend POSTs, when they arrive, then the honeypot field (`_website`) and timing validation (`_form_loaded_at`, <2s or >7d suspicious — `application_handler` helpers reused as-is) apply. Bot-classified posts are silently dropped with a fake-advance (303 to the next question, nothing persisted) — the `/apply` fake-confirmation precedent; no error signal to bots.
+
+**AC7 — Token-hygiene on the page surface.**
+No PostHog/analytics/consent scripts on any `/reference/*` page (the 2026-08-03 token-in-autocapture finding). All pages: `ssr_response.to_sensitive_response` (no-store, no-referrer, noindex) or `to_not_found_response`. Scripts are static-file only (`/static/reference_form.js`, self-origin — no inline JS, no CSP-nonce threading). Unmatched GETs under `/reference/*` never reach the SPA shell (a `["reference", ..]` catch-all GET arm renders the branded unknown-link page — closes the SPA-shell+PostHog token-leak seam for this route family).
+
+**Verify:** server tests — token-state classifier matrix, autosave + resume, TTL/expiry pages, resend (remint + audit + old-token-dead), honeypot/timing silent-drop, SSR render pins, middleware redact/public arms, question-registry integrity (counts 11/8/5, closed vocabs); integration tests for the full session against the Docker test DB; `make test-server` + `make test-integration` green.
+
+## Route table (the router arms this story adds)
+
+| Method + path | Handler | Notes |
+|---|---|---|
+| `GET /reference/:token` | `form_handler.handle_get` | Landing / question (`?q=<id>`) / review / state page per the classifier |
+| `POST /reference/:token/answer` | `form_handler.handle_answer_post` | No-JS per-question save → 303 |
+| `PUT /reference/:token/answer` | `form_handler.handle_answer_put` | JS autosave, JSON in/out |
+| `POST /reference/:token/resend` | `form_handler.handle_resend` | Expired-link re-issue (see AC5) |
+| `GET /reference/:token/..` (any deeper path) | `form_handler.handle_unknown_path` | Branded unknown-link page; MUST sit before the SPA catch-all |
+
+Forward-linked, owned by rc3-4 (NOT registered here): `POST /reference/:token` (submit), `GET|POST /reference/:token/decline`, `GET|POST /reference/:token/stop`, `GET|POST /reference/:token/wrong-person`.
